    "plain": "A universal rollout explicitly targeting rural and remote areas narrows the regional digital divide, which is a real component of inequality. However, an affordability barrier means the poorest households may still be excluded even where coverage arrives, and projected land-value gains flow mainly to property owners.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the affordability gap \u2014 estimated at roughly 2 million people unable to afford gigabit services \u2014 will be closed by social tariffs or left unaddressed, determining whether the poorest benefit at all from the coverage expansion.",
